sec.p:
Baseline clinical assessments were obtained within 30 days before surgery, and postoperative assessments were scheduled for postoperative day 1, day 30, and day 90. The battery of assessments included the following:
Neurological and physical examination;
NPRS;
Patient-Reported Outcome Measurement Information System (PROMIS) measures of pain and function;–
pain intensity;–
neuropathic pain quality;–
nociceptive pain quality;–
pain behavior;–
pain interference;–
PROMIS – cancer – anxiety;–
PROMIS – cancer – depression;–
PROMIS – cancer – fatigue;–
PROMIS – cancer – physical function;
MD Anderson Symptom Inventory for Head and Neck;
Pain Catastrophizing Scale;
concomitant medications.
